          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On March 7, 2022, at 20:43, two witnesses observed in the sky the silent passage of a very bright red point. Its trajectory was straight, and it disappeared behind a building. One of the witnesses had time to film the PAN with his phone. Only one testimony was collected. The witness's description and the video point to the observation of a sky lantern (or flying lantern or Chinese lantern):\n\n- Appearance: rounded point shape,\n- Color: red,\n- Trajectory consistent with the direction and wind reported by the Argenteuil weather station (see weather document) located 4 km from the observation point (witness's reported movement: straight from east to west, station: wind at 78°).\n- The observation took place on a Monday evening, which is not typical for lantern releases, but since the democratization of this type of festive object, days and occasions are less important. Even if a lantern release is less frequent on a Monday than on the weekend, the elements of this observation lead to classifying this case as a very probable observation of a sky lantern.\n\nThe GEIPAN classifies the case as A: very probable observation of a sky lantern.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "9596ac355a778ac53ef0802b0ef33157face75f6f4fb1b8422f6d6771877c35b"
        }
